m is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to 0,$ we require $a<0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cc7d7adc-da21-5b0a-b06f-29905afb7481" "answer-field-3175ebd8-d474-5b16-b3cb-b17b6212db56" "answer-field-d6e8f631-d521-567f-9b3b-b798b0a68214" "answer-field-0c69f5bf-d740-5156-847f-22b4ebc71f50" "answer-field-4f468360-ba03-59ae-8095-aae6ed119b93" "answer-field-5f805543-a610-5f4b-a796-76c04f31765a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cc7d7adc-da21-5b0a-b06f-29905afb7481" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc7d7adc-da21-5b0a-b06f-29905afb7481" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-21842a1e-af52-5181-a20f-521c71b34a69" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d5cf74e7-c791-500f-ba0c-6cd0ce0fad19" "answer-21842a1e-af52-5181-a20f-521c71b34a69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5cf74e7-c791-500f-ba0c-6cd0ce0fad19" :answer/id