pe/select :answer-field/correct "answer-52ec7e21-a1f1-50c8-87b5-0da01b91af28" :answer-field/choices ["answer-52ec7e21-a1f1-50c8-87b5-0da01b91af28" "answer-91e4c64b-2bf8-55e9-88a0-47f602e9e84d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52ec7e21-a1f1-50c8-87b5-0da01b91af28" :answer/id #uuid "52ec7e21-a1f1-50c8-87b5-0da01b91af28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91e4c64b-2bf8-55e9-88a0-47f602e9e84d" :answer/id #uuid "91e4c64b-2bf8-55e9-88a0-47f602e9e84d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-49d51940-1d42-5a6c-821f-8629f9249cb2" :question/id #uuid "49d51940-1d42-5a6c-821f-8629f9249cb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-334301" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =3\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=3>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-20886724-3f12-5b6c-9a63-b9c046281dea" "answer-field-8da7c3d7-9510-5b7c-9e96-9e1ee09eb078"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-20886724-3f12-5b6c-9a63-b9c046281dea" :answer-field/id #uuid "20886724-3f12-5b6c-9a63-b9c046281dea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-27487e30-31ea-50af-a8c0-369003f86c25" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ef940da5-c338-5f7f-aa63-314ee88020a7" "answer-97963b55-7857-5df3-9428-7365708b725e" "answer-d366cefc-ae48-57cd-a166-9dd335e20168" "answer-399a21cc-bc57-5c1a-9a89-23ec395241bc" "answer-1ff6c010-8e48-535b-9136-268227d29260" "answer-27487e30-31ea-50af-a8c0-369003f86c25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef940da5-c338-5f7f-aa63-314ee88020a7" :answer/id #uuid "ef940da5-c338-5f7f-aa63-314ee88020a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97963b55-7857-5df3-9428-7365708b725e" :answer/id #uuid "97963b55-7857-5df3-9428-7365708b725e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d366cefc-ae48-57cd-a166-9dd335e20168" :answer/id #uuid "d366cefc-ae48-57cd-a166-9dd335e20168" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-399a21cc-bc57-5c1a-9a89-23ec395241bc" :answer/id #uuid "399a21cc-bc57-5c1a-9a89-23ec395241bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ff6c010-8e48-535b-9136-268227d29260" :answer/id #uuid "1ff6c010-8e48-535b-9136-268227d29260" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27487e30-31ea-50af-a8c0-369003f86c25" :answer/id #uuid "27487e30-31ea-50af-a8c0-369003f86c25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8da7c3d7-9510-5b7c-9e96-9e1ee09eb078" :answer-field/id #uuid "8da7c3d7-9510-5b7c-9e96-9e1ee09eb078" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-12bc1217-c220-572d-b0d7-d2d34eb5554c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35ef119c-118a-5078-8edf-efc97fc9d855" "answer-e30c39a5-ee5b-5079-97f3-cad9d3c0704d" "answer-12bc1217-c220-572d-b0d7-d2d34eb5554c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35ef119c-118a-5078-8edf-efc97fc9d855" :answer/id #uuid "35ef119c-118a-5078-8edf-efc97fc9d855" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a center" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e30c39a5-ee5b-5079-97f3-cad9d3c0704d" :answer/id #uuid "e30c39a5-ee5b-5079-97f3-cad9d3c0704d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12bc1217-c220-572d-b0d7-d2d34eb5554c" :answer/id #uuid "12bc1217-c220-572d-b0d7-d2d34eb5554c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186308595 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186307814 :answer-field/correct 17592186306470 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-4de2f066-5f99-55ca-83ec-a830f6566d95" :question/id #uuid "4de2f066-5f99-55ca-83ec-a830f6566d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-334303" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =2\\pm 5\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=2>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5e5db6f9-3975-5145-a0d1-b564d7a77d9c" "answer-field-e3d07975-a393-5c75-8820-6b693ddde445"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5e5db6f9-3975-5145-a0d1-b564d7a77d9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5db6f9-3975-5145-a0d1-b564d7a77d9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-dfc2bca0-32a3-55c2-9f6d-6acff395796b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ee678fd-56a0-5e33-a7c3-4084c2657ca8" "answer-010b3e6a-b894-5000-a218-c0e18a932b08" "answer-607896b3-839c-5e51-ac55-d41b15fa7f2d" "answer-a9a75b17-8edb-54a3-a586-17cb8d3b09bc" "answer-26cdebaa-402e-5206-b419-de102d6efa8a" "answer-dfc2bca0-32a3-55c2-9f6d-6acff395796b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ee678fd-56a0-5e33-a7c3-4084c2657ca8" :answer/id #uuid "4ee678fd-56a0-5e33-a7c3-4084c2657ca8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-010b3e6a-b894-5000-a218-c0e18a932b08" :answer/id #uuid "010b3e6a-b894-5000-a218-c0e18a932b08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-607896b3-839c-5e51-ac55-d41b15fa7f2d" :answer/id #uuid "607896b3-839c-5e51-ac55-d41b15fa7f2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9a75b17-8edb-54a3-a586-17cb8d3b09bc" :answer/id #uuid "a9a75b17-8edb-54a3-a586-17cb8d3b09bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26cdebaa-402e-5206-b419-de102d6efa8a" :answer/id #uuid "26cdebaa-402e-5206-b419-de102d6efa8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfc2bca0-32a3-55c2-9f6d-6acff395796b" :answer/id #uuid "dfc2bca0-32a3-55c2-9f6d-6acff395796b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e3d07975-a393-5c75-8820-6b693ddde445" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3d07975-a393-5c75-8820-6b693ddde445" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-dd70c2bc-1b35-5f8d-9da2-4e8f1c15d8fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-923ce9d3-b3c1-58db-8bf6-6828faae079d" "answer-ca0a33be-0f81-5640-8276-2f026a3ba26c" "answer-dd70c2bc-1b35-5f8d-9da2-4e8f1c15d8fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-923ce9d3-b3c1-58db-8bf6-6828faae079d" :answer/id #uuid "923ce9d3-b3c1-58db-8bf6-6828faae079d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a center" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca0a33be-0f81-5640-8276-2f026a3ba26c" :answer/id #uuid "ca0a33be-0f81-5640-8276-2f026a3ba26c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd70c2bc-1b35-5f8d-9da2-4e8f1c15d8fd" :answer/id #uuid "dd70c2bc-1b35-5f8d-9da2-4e8f1c15d8fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167230 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=9x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =1\\pm 6\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186308201 :answer-field/correct 17592186305264 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-c1fcfe84-fe11-5391-abf0-f5881c1a0ef1" :question/id #uuid "c1fcfe84-fe11-5391-abf0-f5881c1a0ef1" :question/math-academy-id "q-334305" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t)-8y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=8x(t)+5y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =5\\pm 8\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=5>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{5t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d312be2-8e22-53a7-b0ac-f747e3a9aeda" "answer-field-73156d6c-fd43-56c5-bed5-47e0532e4a14"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d312be2-8e22-53a7-b0ac-f747e3a9aeda" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d312be2-8e22-53a7-b0ac-f747e3a9aeda" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-44d3d3bc-85e9-5891-a136-208e1a7ae81c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a177b1d-8f4d-5ce4-96d5-0641118ffbd2" "answer-6a53884e-4438-5bc3-ba6b-7c3120bf76ce" "answer-fd467763-82ff-5759-bf17-4bb9e315a854" "answer-61bacac7-6dd5-50c2-956e-a48c2f0f54d3" "answer-59791c19-fe10-5a49-8c0d-1483606ff223" "answer-44d3d3bc-85e9-5891-a136-208e1a7ae81c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a177b1d-8f4d-5ce4-96d5-0641118ffbd2" :answer/id #uuid "2a177b1d-8f4d-5ce4-96d5-0641118ffbd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a53884e-4438-5bc3-ba6b-7c3120bf76ce" :answer/id #uuid "6a53884e-4438-5bc3-ba6b-7c3120bf76ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd467763-82ff-5759-bf17-4bb9e315a854" :answer/id #uuid "fd467763-82ff-5759-bf17-4bb9e315a854" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61bacac7-6dd5-50c2-956e-a48c2f0f54d3" :answer/id #uuid "61bacac7-6dd5-50c2-956e-a48c2f0f54d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59791c19-fe10-5a49-8c0d-1483606ff223" :answer/id #uuid "59791c19-fe10-5a49-8c0d-1483606ff223" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44d3d3bc-85e9-5891-a136-208e1a7ae81c" :answer/id #uuid "44d3d3bc-85e9-5891-a136-208e1a7ae81c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73156d6c-fd43-56c5-bed5-47e0532e4a14" :answer-field/id #uuid "73156d6c-fd43-56c5-bed5-47e0532e4a14" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f6c8c4d4-3353-5b89-8ca9-42cba1be9033" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f18f9e5-125e-52fa-a4bf-f9023b9d06e0" "answer-8c413faf-a70e-5b39-b44f-b5ca5bb38ac8" "answer-f6c8c4d4-3353-5b89-8ca9-42cba1be9033"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f18f9e5-125e-52fa-a4bf-f9023b9d06e0" :answer/id #uuid "4f18f9e5-125e-52fa-a4bf-f9023b9d06e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a center" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c413faf-a70e-5b39-b44f-b5ca5bb38ac8" :answer/id #uuid "8c413faf-a70e-5b39-b44f-b5ca5bb38ac8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6c8c4d4-3353-5b89-8ca9-42cba1be9033" :answer/id #uuid "f6c8c4d4-3353-5b89-8ca9-42cba1be9033" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168010 :tutorial/content "Consider the system of linear differential equations below.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4x(t)+\\frac{1}{2}y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_{1,2} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\pm4\\text{i},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are $\\mathbf{v}_{1,2} = [\\pm \\text{i}, 1]^T,$ respectively. Given that the general solution of the system is\n![](images/d1/d13abb97b171049a17544fcb312b71d2da3d9294788c1aebe7aa969e99b7819c.svg)\nwe are interested in sketching the phase portrait of the system of differential equations given above.\n\nIf we set $c_1 = 1$ and $c_2 = 0$ in the general solution of the system, we obtain the particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x={e}^{t/2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ y={e}^{t/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\dfrac{\\pi}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.78$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.78$ | $1.22$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/4f/4f9da4b66977b98b983477d22abb6e00135ea0e1bfa9f785cd0a62d674a7b782.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\sin(4t)| \\leq 1$ and $|\\cos(4t)| \\leq 1,$ but $e^{t/2} \\to \\infty$ as $t \\to \\infty.$ Thus, the obtained curve is unbounded. So, we have a spiral that is traversed counterclockwise.\n\nAgain, since $e^{t/2} \\to \\infty$ as $t \\to \\infty,$ the spiral is traversed toward infinity as $t \\to \\infty.$\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/62/62380812d6fbe4e28531a455814296a4969a0744fb28a94a5e2d7c588ec5cfc4.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168025 :tutorial/content "Finally, let’s summarize what we’ve learned so far.\n\nAgain, we are considering a linear system\n![](images/65/6597a81f818926afff9056180de0e12357ef7631be093aba32626a7461079c18.svg)\nwhere the eigenvalues of a $2 \\times 2$ matrix $A$ are\n\n$$\n\\lambda_{1,2}=a\\pm bi,\n\\qquad b\\neq 0.\n$$\n\nAs for the classification of the equilibrium at the origin, we get the following:\n\n- The type of the curve is determined by the parameter $a{:}$\n\n- If $a=0,$ we have bounded closed curves (ellipses/circles).\n\n- If $a \\neq 0,$ we have spirals.\n\n- The stability is determined by the sign of $a{:}$\n\n- If $a>0,$ we have an **unstable spiral** (source).\n\n- If $a<0,$ we have a **stable spiral** (sink).\n\n- If $a=0,$ we have a **center**.\n\n**Note:** The center is a *stable* equilibrium but not *asymptotically stable* since trajectories do not converge to it.\n\nLet's see an example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167012 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
